From 1b8fd63c5c2d55005b3ed2c1298cc775fa8bd295 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yannick Serafini <yannick.serafini@wifx.net>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 14:20:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] Anchor the UTC reference to the OS wall clock

rt_utcOffset is captured once in rt_ini() and never re-derived from the OS
clock. Without PPS its only later update is the drift correction in
ts_updateTimesync(), which steers it to the concentrator counter. Any error
present at process start therefore becomes permanent and the published UTC
drifts at the TCXO's rate error: measured in the field, a constant offset of
0.8 to 5 s plus a residual slope of 3 to 5 ppm.

Add sys_utcTrusted() to query the kernel NTP discipline state with adjtimex(),
and a self-scheduling loop in timesync.c that compares rt_getUTC() against
sys_utc() while the clock is trusted, slewing small errors and stepping large
ones after confirmation. The loop releases the reference to the PPS logic, and
both the drift steering and router_config MuxTime stand down while it owns it.

Rationale, precedence between the writers of rt_utcOffset, parameters, log
lines and field measurements: doc/wifx/utc-anchor.md

Signed-off-by: Yannick Serafini <yannick.serafini@wifx.net>
